module gunbc.seed_closed_vocabulary_wildcard_census

import std.types { String }

// WHAT THIS CARRIER IS. The .dag substrate's vocabularies are CLOSED coproducts, and
// closure is a guarantee: a fold over one either names every member or fails to compile.
// A seed-side Rust `match` over the SAME vocabulary that ends in a catch-all discards
// exactly that guarantee -- the wildcard absorbs every form the author did not think of,
// including forms added to the .dag authority afterwards, and answers for them. This is
// DESIGN section 5's fabricated-plausible-output failure sitting one layer below the
// compiler's own claims, and DESIGN section 4b's rung honesty applied to the seed: a
// projection that ANSWERS where it cannot READ reports a state it never observed.
//
// The rows below are the sites this census turns on: six that still ANSWER WITH A VALUE,
// one recorded as faithfully mirroring its own .dag authority's collapse so that it is not
// re-found as a seed defect, and one this change CLOSED -- kept beside the open ones so the
// closure is visible rather than inferred from an absence. Sites whose catch-all was always
// the honest classification of everything remaining are not rows here. The
// full extraction is a measurement and lives in the change that landed this file, not
// here; a ledger of sites that are already correct would be a second representation of
// the source with no consumer (DESIGN section 2).
//
// THE MEASUREMENT, with its subject and its instrument, because a census without either
// is a number nobody can re-derive.
//
// SUBJECT: every .rs file outside target/ in this repository at 026a709a71636d60df325f9183b78febff22901d,
// partitioned into HAND-WRITTEN and GENERATED by a header scan (generated mirrors carry a
// generated / do-not-edit line in their first four lines). Only hand-written files are in
// scope: a wildcard in an emitted mirror is a fact about its .dag source, and the fix
// belongs there.
//
// INSTRUMENT: a brace-balanced extractor over comment- and string-blanked source, keeping
// matches whose arm patterns name a type that also appears as a closed coproduct
// declaration in the .dag corpus (4193 such vocabularies) and whose LAST arm is `_` or a
// bare binder. Result: 794 catch-all matches over closed .dag vocabularies corpus-wide,
// 92 of them in hand-written seed Rust.
//
// THE INSTRUMENT'S RECALL WAS WRONG ONCE AND IS RECORDED RATHER THAN REPAIRED SILENTLY.
// Its first form reported 48 hand-written sites. Hand-verifying a site it should have
// found -- `marshal_decl_fact_node`, which is one of the rows below -- showed it dropped
// every match whose second-to-last arm has a BLOCK body, because the pattern text it
// split out then began with the block's closing brace and no longer looked like a
// catch-all. Repairing that single class took the count from 48 to 92. So the honest
// statement about recall is not that it is complete; it is that one recall class was
// found by hand-checking a known positive, which is the only reason the other 44 are
// here, and no instrument has established that a third class does not exist.
//
// WHY MATCHES OVER THE INTERPRETER'S OWN `Value` ARE NOT IN THIS CENSUS, stated here
// rather than left as an omission a reader would have to detect. The extraction also
// finds a large population of catch-alls over `v1_interpreter::Value` -- the seed's
// runtime value union. That type is declared in Rust and nowhere in .dag. It carries no
// closure guarantee for a wildcard to discard, and its catch-alls are honest totality: a
// projection that wants a record and is handed an integer has genuinely classified its
// input, and the arm IS the answer rather than a substitute for one. The distinction
// this census turns on is therefore not the shape of the match -- fabricating and total
// catch-alls are indistinguishable at the site -- but whether the scrutinee's vocabulary
// is closed by an authority the seed is supposed to be answerable to.
type SeedWildcardDisposition =
    FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: String }
  | MirrorsAuthorityArm
  | EveryFormNamed

// One hand-written seed site whose catch-all over a closed .dag vocabulary answers with a
// value instead of refusing. Cited by SYMBOL (DESIGN section 3): the enclosing Rust
// function and the file that declares it, never a line offset.
type SeedWildcardSite {
  file: String
  symbol: String
  vocabulary: String
  vocabulary_authority: String
  unhandled_forms: String
  reachability: String
  harm: String
  disposition: SeedWildcardDisposition
  next_trigger: String
}

// REACHABILITY IS AN INFERENCE ON EVERY ROW BELOW AND IS LABELLED AS ONE. The source-form
// counts are measured on the subject above; the mapping from a source form to the
// `Connective` or `ItemKind` the walk sees is READ OFF THE PARSER
// (`v1_compiler_parse` `parse_type_body_from_prefix` / `parse_type_body_after_eq`,
// `v1_compiler_infer_items` `item_kind`), not observed by execution. A row that says a
// form is reachable is saying the code path admits it, not that a run was watched
// reaching it.
data seed_closed_vocabulary_wildcard_sites: List<SeedWildcardSite> = [
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/coproduct_reflection.rs",
    symbol: "concept_decl_node",
    vocabulary: "Connective",
    vocabulary_authority: "v1.core Connective",
    unhandled_forms: "NoConnective, Arrow",
    reachability: "reached: 100 single-name alias type declarations parse to NoConnective and 7 fn-type aliases parse through the same non-variant path (source-form counts over dag/ and src/v2/ at the subject ref)",
    harm: "every alias declaration in the corpus is marshalled into concept_decl_facts as the UNIT type node -- the same node a genuinely empty record produces -- so a lens reading these facts cannot distinguish an alias from a fieldless record, and reads an alias as carrying no structure at all",
    disposition: FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: "unit_type_node" },
    next_trigger: "the alias and arrow forms marshal to their own projections, or decl_facts declares a typed unmarshalled-form node naming the connective; a bare refusal is NOT available here because the arm is on the corpus-wide walk and would stop every consumer"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/coproduct_reflection.rs",
    symbol: "marshal_decl_fact_node",
    vocabulary: "ItemKind",
    vocabulary_authority: "v1.items ItemKind",
    unhandled_forms: "ServiceItem, OtherItem",
    reachability: "reached: decl_facts_corpus_walk emits a row for every item at every one of the six kinds -- its own sort key enumerates all six -- and 110 service declarations exist under dag/ and src/v2/ at the subject ref",
    harm: "every service declaration enters decl_facts as the unit type node, so the fact population states that a service declares nothing",
    disposition: FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: "unit_type_node" },
    next_trigger: "same as concept_decl_node: a service projection, or a typed unmarshalled-form node naming the kind"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/coproduct_reflection.rs",
    symbol: "marshal_export_signature_node",
    vocabulary: "ItemKind",
    vocabulary_authority: "v1.items ItemKind",
    unhandled_forms: "ServiceItem, OtherItem",
    reachability: "reached: shares decl_facts_for_roots with marshal_decl_fact_node, so the same population arrives",
    harm: "an export signature for a service renders as the unit node, so an interface summary derived from these facts under-states the module's surface without saying so",
    disposition: FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: "unit_type_node" },
    next_trigger: "the service export signature is modelled, or the row carries a typed unmarshalled-form node"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/data_initializer_identity.rs",
    symbol: "marshal_data_initializer_projection_for_item",
    vocabulary: "ExprData",
    vocabulary_authority: "v1.core ExprData",
    unhandled_forms: "every form except ExprRecordLit and ExprVar -- 20 of the 22 members",
    reachability: "reached: a data declaration initialised by a list literal, a call or an interpolation is ordinary and common in this corpus",
    harm: "the projection answers NotVariantValue, which is a POSITIVE claim that the initializer was inspected and is not a variant value; the state it should report is that the form has no projection rule at all, and the two are indistinguishable downstream",
    disposition: FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: "DataInitializerValueResolution::NotVariantValue" },
    next_trigger: "a distinct resolution arm for an initializer form the projection carries no rule for, so the unread case stops being reported as a read one"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs",
    symbol: "collect_argv_input_refs",
    vocabulary: "ExprData",
    vocabulary_authority: "v1.core ExprData",
    unhandled_forms: "every form except ExprVar and ExprStringInterp",
    reachability: "reached by the same construction as extdeps_argv_expr_token, which this change repaired: the argv position admits any expression and a call there typechecks",
    harm: "an argv element the walk cannot read contributes NO input reference, and the dead-parameter reading folds over exactly these references -- so a declared input genuinely used through an unread form is reported as dead",
    disposition: FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: "no reference, silently" },
    next_trigger: "the same repair extdeps_argv_expr_token took -- refuse by form name -- once the ShellTransportOperationCensusRow producer carries a refusal channel to its consumer"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs",
    symbol: "extdeps_argv_expr_token",
    vocabulary: "ExprData and LiteralValue",
    vocabulary_authority: "v1.core ExprData and std.syntax LiteralValue",
    unhandled_forms: "every form except ExprLiteral(LitStr), ExprVar and ExprStringInterp",
    reachability: "PROVEN BY EXECUTION ON THE LIVE CORPUS, not inferred, and it is the only row in this census whose arm was watched being reached. Two live sites: extdeps.git git.Core.DiffUnified0 argv[3] and git.Core.DiffNameStatus argv[4], both ExprCall. The second was invisible to the refusal run, which aborted at the first -- it appeared only once the arm announced instead of refusing, which is the argument for announcing at all. Both operations are named in test.claim.operation_argv_corpus_witness s counted expression residue, so this is the same population the materialization side already types, not a new class",
    harm: "an argv element the projection cannot read is rendered as the EMPTY STRING, and no policy predicate matches an empty token, so a leak carried by an unreadable form is reported as clean. The two readings of one corpus therefore disagree: v2.std.operation_argv counts the same elements as typed ArgvRowExpressionResidue -- seven operations, pinned in test.claim.operation_argv_corpus_witness -- while this census renders them as clean tokens",
    disposition: FabricatedSubstitution { substituted: "the empty string, now announced per occurrence as a located [extdeps-argv-unprojectable] line rather than absorbed silently" },
    next_trigger: "ExtdepsTransportArgvFact carries a typed projection (ProjectedToken / UnprojectableForm) the way the materialization row already does, and the policy fold reads it -- at which point the empty string is unwritable and the boundary refuses. THE HARD REFUSAL WAS BUILT AND DELIBERATELY NOT LANDED: it stops corpus_git_policy_leak_defused_holds, and that red is not closable by the author who causes it, because the argv-call population is another lane's counted debt. A wall whose only reachable green is someone else's modelling change is not a wall this change may raise"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "dag/tools/self_host_std_bridge_shims/v2_std_node.rs",
    symbol: "well_formed",
    vocabulary: "Connective",
    vocabulary_authority: "v2.std.node Connective",
    unhandled_forms: "Cardinality and Instantiation were answered well-formed; both are now checked, and Arrow is named as a declared residue",
    reachability: "the arm was reachable for any node of either form; no run was watched reaching it, so the defect is established against the authority rather than against an observed input",
    harm: "CLOSED by this change. The authority connective_edges_conform requires count(children) >= 1 for BOTH Cardinality and Instantiation, so an empty node of either form passed a check the authority fails -- a fail-open in the seed-linked normalize gate, one connective away from the case review 44739 caught in the same function",
    disposition: EveryFormNamed,
    next_trigger: "Arrow still answers true because the authority routes it to arrow_body_edges_conform, which this bridge does not carry; it dissolves with the bridge itself when the emitted v2 std closure compiles and the authority's fold is used directly"
  },
  SeedWildcardSite {
    file: "src/v1/stage0/src/v2_compiler_target_carriers.rs",
    symbol: "target_fidelity_quotient_optional",
    vocabulary: "NamedEdgeTargetLookup",
    vocabulary_authority: "v2.std.node NamedEdgeTargetLookup",
    unhandled_forms: "Ambiguous, Absent",
    reachability: "reached whenever the named edge is absent, which is the ordinary case",
    harm: "an AMBIGUOUS named edge is answered as ABSENT, so a target model carrying two fidelity quotients reads as carrying none and decodes Lossless",
    disposition: MirrorsAuthorityArm,
    next_trigger: "NOT this lane's row to fix, and it is recorded so nobody re-finds it as a seed defect: the .dag authority v2.compiler.07_target_carriers target_fidelity_quotient_optional performs the SAME collapse over find_named_child's Rejected arm. The seed is a faithful mirror; the conflation lives in the model and any repair belongs there first"
  }
]
